1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,750
Feeling hungry?
感觉饿了吗？

2
00:00:01,750 --> 00:00:09,420
If you’re feeling peckish or famished, what’s the easiest way to satisfy your hunger?
要是你有点饥肠辘辘或是饿得前胸贴后背，满足食欲最简单的办法是什么呢？

3
00:00:09,420 --> 00:00:18,960
Many of us will reach for a takeaway menu and order some delicious – but possibly unhealthy – food.
很多人会拿起外卖菜单，点上一些美味却可能不太健康的食物。

4
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:29,080
And our increasingly busy and hectic lives add to our need to buy ready-made food on the go or delivered to home.
如今我们的生活越来越忙碌紧凑，这也让我们更需要购买现成的食物，要么在外随手解决，要么直接配送到家。

5
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:38,630
Eating options are endless, and new technology means we can feed our cravings at the push of a button.
吃的选择数不胜数，新技术的发展更是让我们只需按一下按钮，就能满足口腹之欲。

6
00:00:38,630 --> 00:00:56,490
Takeaway delivery apps make ordering food quick and convenient, and during the recent coronavirus crisis, it provided a lifeline to those stuck at home with nothing to cook or who lacked the skills to prepare a meal for themselves.
外卖配送应用让点餐变得快捷方便，在最近的新冠疫情期间，它更是成了许多人的救命稻草——那些被困在家、没东西可做，或是根本不会做饭的人，全靠外卖度日。

7
00:00:56,490 --> 00:01:12,360
It’s estimated that in the UK alone, people eat three million takeaway meals a day, and the three biggest delivery apps together offer a choice of 100 cuisines from 60,000 restaurants.
据估计，仅在英国，人们每天就要吃掉300万份外卖，三大外卖平台加起来，能提供来自6万家餐厅的100种风味美食。

8
00:01:12,360 --> 00:01:27,110
Amelia Brophy, Head of UK Data Products at YouGov, told the BBC that its research “suggests that the frequency of takeaways ordered is expected to increase in the future.”
舆观调查网英国数据产品主管阿米莉亚·布罗菲在接受BBC采访时表示，他们的研究显示“未来外卖的下单频率预计还会上升”。

9
00:01:27,110 --> 00:01:36,750
It’s no wonder we are tempted to skip the grocery shopping, bypass the kitchen, and tuck into something that someone else has prepared.
难怪我们会忍不住想跳过买菜这一步，绕开厨房，直接大快朵颐别人做好的饭菜。

10
00:01:36,750 --> 00:01:47,790
But ordering a deep crust pizza, a spicy curry or a box of noodles, can come at a price both financially and to our health.
但点一份厚底披萨、一份辛辣咖喱或是一盒面条，代价是双重的——既花钱，又损害健康。

11
00:01:47,790 --> 00:02:00,320
Eating too much processed and unhealthy fast food has some effect on obesity and the risk of developing certain metabolic and cardiovascular diseases.
吃太多加工过的不健康快餐，会增加肥胖风险，还可能诱发某些代谢性疾病和心血管疾病。

12
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:09,560
A few years ago, The BBC Good Food Nation Survey found that most people ate fast food on average two days per week.
几年前，《BBC美食国度调查报告》发现，大多数人平均每周吃两天快餐。

13
00:02:09,560 --> 00:02:18,010
But, in the 16 to 20-year-old category, one in six ate fast food at least twice a day.
而在16到20岁的年龄段，六分之一的人每天至少吃两次快餐。

14
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:28,260
Of course, reducing salt, sugar and fat is one way to make takeaway food healthier, as well as offering smaller portion sizes.
当然，让外卖变得更健康的方法之一，就是减少盐、糖和脂肪的含量，同时提供小份餐食。

15
00:02:28,260 --> 00:02:38,980
But the best advice you might want to take away from this Takeaway English is to find a recipe book and try making your own nutritious meal.
不过，从这篇“外卖英语”里，你能得到的最佳建议是：找一本食谱，试着自己做一顿营养均衡的饭菜。

16
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:45,780
And if you haven’t got time, try ordering a healthier alternative from the menu.
要是实在没时间，那就从菜单上选一个更健康的菜品吧。
